WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.462
Stage seven is a runbook, not a flag day,
and that's what keeps rollback possible.

2
00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:08.022
Waves are defined by attribute values,

3
00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:11.301
so each wave is a query
whose groups already exist.

4
00:00:11.301 --> 00:00:15.850
Start with a pilot division, and keep
each one drift-clean before the next.

5
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:20.313
Do leaver automation first, because
revocation is where the risk is.

6
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:23.962
The gate is the strip across
the top: a signed report,

7
00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:29.262
a dry run with writes off, then seven
days in which every change traces to HR.

8
00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.425
Only then does the ticket path close.

9
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:35.063
And disable, never delete,
so you can always go back.

10
00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:36.220
Then, drift.
